@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Public booking flow

# The public guest booking flow at /book/{slug}. There is no login here -
# the tenant (Business) is resolved from the slug in
# BookingsController::beforeFilter(), which 404s on an unknown slug.
#
# Replace `demo-salon`, service id `1` and staff id `1` below with real
# values from your own seeded data - run `make seed` first, or create a
# Business/Service/User via the admin dashboard.

### List the services a Business offers
GET {{baseUrl}}/book/demo-salon/

### Show which staff can perform a given Service
GET {{baseUrl}}/book/demo-salon/service/1

### Show available slots for a Service/staff pairing on a given date
# `date` defaults to today if omitted. Slots are staff hours minus
# existing bookings minus the configured buffer (SlotFinder).
GET {{baseUrl}}/book/demo-salon/service/1/staff/1?date=2026-09-21

### Submit a guest booking
# First GET the form above to obtain a real `_csrfToken` value and its
# matching `csrfToken` cookie (CakePHP's CsrfProtectionMiddleware requires
# both to match) - the values below are illustrative only and will be
# rejected as-is. `slot` must be one of the `H:i` times the GET response
# lists as available; on success this creates the Customer (found or
# created by email), creates the Booking, sends the confirmation email
# with an .ics attachment, and queues the reminder job.
POST {{baseUrl}}/book/demo-salon/service/1/staff/1?date=2026-09-21
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Cookie: csrfToken=REPLACE_WITH_COOKIE_VALUE

_csrfToken=REPLACE_WITH_FORM_TOKEN&name=Jane+Doe&email=jane%40example.com&phone=07700900000&slot=09%3A00
